From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:47:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: macsmc-input - confirm a lid-open report
 during system sleep

On the J716s (MacBook Pro 16-inch, M5 Pro) closing the lid starts a
suspend through logind, and the system is awake again 0.7 s later. The
SMC's own syslog shows the cause: about 230 ms after the close
("SMC HID Event: 03 01 00") it reports the lid open ("03 00 01", event
0x72030001, the same bytes as a real opening) while the lid stays shut,
at the same moment as the trackpad coprocessor logs "Sending Cumulus
Report to enter Dependent Mode" (Cumulus is the touch AFE). The driver
takes the report at face value: it is in the sleep window, so it reports
a hard wakeup, pm_system_wakeup() aborts the suspend or ends
suspend-to-idle, and logind then reads "Lid opened".

In the sleep window, between .prepare and .complete, check a lid-open
report before passing it on. Read the SMC's lid key MSLD, the one probe
reads the initial state from: if it says closed, the report is dropped.
If it agrees but the sleep has run for lid_settle_ms or less, the report
does not wake the system either. lid_settle_ms is 2000 on the J716s, the
only machine where the false report has been seen, and 0 everywhere
else, so other machines keep waking on the first open report that MSLD
confirms; the lid_wake_settle_ms module parameter overrides it at load
time (-1 = per-machine default, 0 = never hold). The machine is matched
with of_machine_is_compatible() because macsmc-input is an MFD cell
without a node of its own. A held-back report leaves SW_LID closed, and
.complete reports MSLD again, so the switch matches the SMC after any
wakeup. Each decision is logged with the event, the time into the sleep
and MSLD, so a test can tell which check fired.

The notifier runs in the SMC's RTKit worker and the SMC's replies are
taken from the mailbox interrupt (recv_message_early), so reading a key
there does not wait on the worker. The sleep time is taken from
CLOCK_BOOTTIME, which includes the time suspend-to-idle spends with
timekeeping suspended.

What this does not fix, on the J716s: if MSLD agrees with the false
report, the SMC already counts the lid as open, and the real opening
that follows may send no event at all. The system then stays asleep
until a key, a trackpad click or the power button wakes it, instead of
waking at once.

Not changed: lid-close reports, the power button, and any lid-open
report outside the sleep window.

Tested on the J716s with logind suspending on lid close (s2idle): the
close sleeps ("Timekeeping suspended for 39.477 seconds") and the real
opening wakes it through the confirm path ("lid open 72030001 at +40069
ms in sleep, MSLD=0: wakeup"). No spurious report came during that
sleep, so the hold-back path has not run on hardware yet.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9423412263b8d529c6cb609713b19faa05eaf59c)
[Dylan: ported onto the J604 series, which already keeps SW_LID unreported
 through a sleep from PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE and resynchronises it from MSLD at
 PM_POST_SUSPEND and .complete. Took the MSLD confirm and the settle window
 (0 on the J604); dropped lid_held, lid_lock and the .complete resync, which
 ours already covers. The sleep start is taken at PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE and when
 going back to sleep after a dark wake.]
[dylan: carried from aurora-silicon/linux 9423412263b8; one co-author trailer of the original message is not reproduced here, see the upstream commit for the full text]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 65 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c b/drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c
index fb3fe3fdb6..83af15fe7c 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/macsmc-input.c
@@ -10,11 +10,21 @@
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/input.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/core.h>
+#include <linux/ktime.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/macsmc.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/reboot.h>
 #include <linux/suspend.h>
 
+#define LID_WAKE_SETTLE_MS_J716S	2000
+
+static int lid_wake_settle_ms = -1;
+module_param(lid_wake_settle_ms, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(lid_wake_settle_ms,
+		 "A lid-open report this many ms or less after system sleep starts does not wake the system (0 = always wake, default: 2000 on the J716s, 0 elsewhere)");
+
 /**
  * struct macsmc_input
  * @dev: Underlying struct device for the input sub-device
@@ -24,6 +34,8 @@
  * @pm_nb: Notifier block for the start and end of a system suspend
  * @wakeup_mode: Set to true when system is suspended and power button events should wake it
  * @dark: Going back to sleep from a dark wake: the lid is read again before it
+ * @lid_settle_ms: Window after system sleep starts in which a lid-open report is held back
+ * @sleep_start: CLOCK_BOOTTIME at which this system sleep started
  */
 struct macsmc_input {
 	struct device *dev;
@@ -33,6 +45,8 @@ struct macsmc_input {
 	struct notifier_block pm_nb;
 	bool wakeup_mode;
 	bool dark;
+	unsigned int lid_settle_ms;
+	ktime_t sleep_start;
 };
 
 #define SMC_EV_BTN 0x7201
@@ -84,10 +98,53 @@ static void macsmc_input_event_button(struct macsmc_input *smcin, unsigned long
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * On the J716s the SMC has reported the lid open (event 0x72030001, the same
+ * bytes as a real opening) while the lid stayed shut, about 230 ms after the
+ * close that started the suspend and in step with the trackpad coprocessor
+ * moving its AFE to "Dependent Mode". Taken at face value, that report ends
+ * the suspend the close started. So in the sleep window an open report wakes
+ * the system only if the SMC's lid key agrees and the sleep has run for
+ * longer than lid_settle_ms, which is nonzero only where this was seen.
+ */
+static bool macsmc_input_lid_wake_ok(struct macsmc_input *smcin, unsigned long event)
+{
+	s64 ms = ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get_boottime(), smcin->sleep_start);
+	u8 closed;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = apple_smc_read_u8(smcin->smc, SMC_KEY(MSLD), &closed);
+	if (ret < 0) {
+		dev_warn(smcin->dev, "lid open %08lx at +%lld ms in sleep, MSLD read failed: %d\n",
+			 event, ms, ret);
+		closed = 0;
+	}
+
+	if (closed) {
+		dev_info(smcin->dev, "lid open %08lx at +%lld ms in sleep, MSLD=%u: ignored\n",
+			 event, ms, closed);
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	if (smcin->lid_settle_ms && ms <= smcin->lid_settle_ms) {
+		dev_info(smcin->dev, "lid open %08lx at +%lld ms in sleep, MSLD=0, within %u ms: no wakeup\n",
+			 event, ms, smcin->lid_settle_ms);
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	dev_info(smcin->dev, "lid open %08lx at +%lld ms in sleep, MSLD=0: wakeup\n", event, ms);
+	return true;
+}
+
 static void macsmc_input_event_lid(struct macsmc_input *smcin, unsigned long event)
 {
 	u8 lid_state = !!((event >> 8) & 0xff);
 
+	/* Held back: SW_LID is resynchronised from MSLD when the sleep ends. */
+	if (READ_ONCE(smcin->wakeup_mode) && !lid_state &&
+	    !macsmc_input_lid_wake_ok(smcin, event))
+		return;
+
 	pm_wakeup_dev_event(smcin->dev, 0, (smcin->wakeup_mode && !lid_state));
 	/* Through a sleep, .complete reports where the lid ended up. */
 	if (smcin->wakeup_mode)
@@ -125,6 +182,7 @@ static int macsmc_input_pm_notify(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long actio
 	struct macsmc_input *smcin = container_of(nb, struct macsmc_input, pm_nb);
 
 	if (action == PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE) {
+		smcin->sleep_start = ktime_get_boottime();
 		WRITE_ONCE(smcin->wakeup_mode, true);
 	} else if (action == PM_POST_SUSPEND) {
 		u8 val;
@@ -177,6 +235,12 @@ static int macsmc_input_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	smcin->smc = smc;
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, smcin);
 
+	/* No OF node of its own: the false report has been seen on the J716s only. */
+	if (lid_wake_settle_ms >= 0)
+		smcin->lid_settle_ms = lid_wake_settle_ms;
+	else if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716s"))
+		smcin->lid_settle_ms = LID_WAKE_SETTLE_MS_J716S;
+
 	smcin->input = devm_input_allocate_device(&pdev->dev);
 	if (!smcin->input)
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -258,6 +322,7 @@ static int macsmc_input_pm_prepare(struct device *dev)
 	/* A lid opened as the dark wake ended may have sent its event already. */
 	if (smcin->dark) {
 		smcin->dark = false;
+		smcin->sleep_start = ktime_get_boottime();
 		if (apple_smc_key_exists(smcin->smc, SMC_KEY(MSLD)) &&
 		    apple_smc_read_u8(smcin->smc, SMC_KEY(MSLD), &val) >= 0 && !val) {
 			dev_info(dev, "the lid opened during a dark wake: not sleeping again\n");
